  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Belize has adopted an integrated approach to decent work</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With ILO support, Belize has introduced a landmark Occupational Safety and Health (OSH) Bill to strengthen worker protection nationwide. Replacing the outdated Factories Act, the Bill aligns with ILO Conventions No. 155 and No. 187 and reflects priorities in Belize&#x2019;s Decent Work Country Programme 2024&#x2013;2029.

Key reforms include the creation of a National OSH Advisory Committee and a dedicated OSH Inspectorate, with provisions for a future standalone OSH Authority. The Bill defines clear responsibilities for all workplace actors and introduces whistleblower protections, mandatory incident reporting, and workplace safety committees. Enforcement tools such as improvement notices and penalties aim to ensure compliance.

This modern legislation is expected to reduce workplace accidents, improve productivity, and strengthen Belize&#x2019;s social protection systems.</narrative>
  </description>
